 "poem": "How the falling leaves fall on our\nCurved fence - how they are fallen away\nIn small clusters, scattered\nAbove and below it everywhere\nFrom field to field: - so much as our\nLife's earthlings have gathered there before,\nThe stars had outlasted our\nStriving years; - nor can we trace our\nLines of life from one star into\nAnother if each cluster\nFallen is not worth our\nThoughts that cling like a love flower,",
